{
  "requirement": "The `habeas` CLI MUST use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Implementation.** The requirement says the `habeas` CLI MUST use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options. `src/main.rs` does this completely.\n- `Cargo.toml` depends on `clap` 4.6.7 with the `derive` feature. `src/main.rs` imports `clap::{ArgGroup, Parser, Subcommand}`.\n- `Cli` (`#[derive(Parser)]`, name `habeas`) is marked `{impl}`. `Command`, `MdbookCommand` and `HookCommand` (`#[derive(Subcommand)]`) are also marked `{impl}`.\n- The `Command` enum defines every command and option with clap:\n  - `mdbook` with its `supports` subcommand, `setup --path`, `status [--all] [--verbose] [selection]`, and `info <selection>`.\n  - `author` with its `author-evidence` alias, `--all`, `--config`, `--stdout`, and `-v/--verbose`, plus the `ArgGroup` and `conflicts_with` rules.\n  - The hidden `hook` command, and `add-input` with its target and mode `ArgGroup`s.\n- `main` calls `Cli::parse()`, marked `{impl}`, and dispatches only on the parsed values.\n- Argument parsing is clap-only. A search found no other `fn main`, `[[bin]]`, `Parser` use for CLI parsing, or `env::args` use. The only binary is `habeas` (`src/main.rs`).\n- Other behavior in this code is attributed to other requirements through their own `{impl}` comments: `cli.add_input*`, `authoring.*`, `configuration.*`, `cli.status` and the rest. This requirement does not cover that behavior, and the `{impl}` markers are complete.\n\n**Tests.**\n- `tests/cli.rs::clap_defines_commands_options_and_usage_errors` runs the real binary and checks:\n  - `--help` output starts with `Usage: habeas <COMMAND>` and lists every public command.\n  - The hidden `hook` command is absent from the help.\n  - `status --help` shows `--all` and `--verbose`.\n  - The `author-evidence` alias resolves to `author`.\n  - Three usage-error cases (an unknown option, a missing required argument, and conflicting arguments) exit with code 2, include clap's message, and print the `Usage:` line.\n- `tests/commands.rs::add_input_requires_one_target_and_mode_and_resets_changed_records` is also marked `{test}` for this requirement. It verifies that clap's `ArgGroup`s reject two targets, two modes, no target, and no mode. Each case exits with code 2, prints `Usage: habeas add-input`, and writes nothing.\n\nTogether the tests cover the interesting points: help generation, the alias, hidden commands, groups and conflicts, and failure exit codes and messages. The tests plausibly could not be passed by a non-clap parser, because they check clap-specific output and exit codes.\n\nNo gaps or FIXMEs were found.",
  "references": "c3c091a5580a2047da77d06cee9d1f88dddd56e8faa5831de3f402b557cd31a4",
